1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:17,540
Aiming for a certain day
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:24,660
I kicked a pebble and my shoe flew off too,

3
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:32,960
onto the head of the carpenter
I had put in a chokehold.

4
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:39,120
I got laughed at for
still acting like a kid.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I chase after energy somewhere,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,280
a yawn or two changes nothing.

7
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:53,160
The streetscape feels strangely gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:07,440
From the pointed-hat water basin,
the sunset falls toward the great sky.

9
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:19,720
Tomorrow it will end like this too, and in
Katsushika Shibamata, we'll say we're happy again.

10
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:22,400
Only after losing it did I realize.

11
00:01:22,400 --> 00:01:24,680
Because I'm a foolish guy.

12
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:31,000
Farewell, Chief Ohara.

13
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:38,520
Hey!

14
00:01:39,500 --> 00:01:42,480
Hey, you! Pay up!

15
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,620
Officer, grab that guy!

16
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,500
He's skipped out on his bill!

17
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:50,200
He's running away!

18
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:55,200
Ah! Don't let him get away, Ryotsu!
Catch him no matter what!

19
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,420
Understood!

20
00:01:56,420 --> 00:01:57,960
Seriously!?

21
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:20,540
Eeeeeeeh!

22
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:23,180
Aaaaaaah!

23
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:29,320
Eeeeeeeh!

24
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,940
Eeeeeeeh!

25
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:32,180
Eeeeeeeh!

26
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:32,820
Eeeeeeeh!

27
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:34,940
Eeeeeeeh!

28
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:35,280
Eeeeeeeh!

29
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:10,060
So, how about that? Admit defeat!

30
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:10,800
I admit defeat.

31
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,800
Chief, as you can see,
I've arrested the culprit.

32
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:24,920
What happened to you, Chief?
Look at your appearance!

33
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,980
You idiot!

34
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:30,320
Who told you to go that far?

35
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:33,260
You really don't know when to stop, do you?

36
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:36,580
After all, I've arrested three people.

37
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:41,340
I've told you to use your head, not just your body.
Use your head!

38
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,860
Who do you think is going
to clean up this mess?

39
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:48,380
Ryo-chan's basically the type who acts before he thinks,
isn't he?

40
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:50,740
Even when I cross the road,

41
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:55,080
I look right, then left,
then right and left again,

42
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:57,080
and then I look up before crossing.

43
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,880
Why would you look up?

44
00:03:59,380 --> 00:04:01,640
Because a meteorite might fall on me!

45
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,160
Yes, Kameari Park police box speaking.

46
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,580
Chief, it's a call from the station chief.

47
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:07,620
Mm.

48
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,080
Don't be ridiculous,
if I spend the whole day doing that,

49
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:10,660
This is Ohara.

50
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:12,380
I'd only have a third
of the day left to use!

51
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:16,220
Me, filling in for the team
leader at the Sanchome police box?

52
00:04:16,940 --> 00:04:20,460
Well, yes, understood.

53
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,960
What's wrong, Chief?

54
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:35,060
The Third Block police box is the one where the team
leader was hospitalized for a sudden illness, right?

55
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:37,180
Yes, that's what this is about.

56
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:40,540
I'm going to be acting team
leader there for a while.

57
00:04:40,540 --> 00:04:42,640
So what about this police box?

58
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:44,980
The only one left to
fill in here is the Chief.

59
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,160
Yay!

60
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:49,400
What do you mean, "yay"?

61
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,400
Well...

62
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,660
No, it's not that I'm
glad the Chief is gone...

63
00:04:52,660 --> 00:04:55,160
I'm not thinking that I'm relieved
or that it's nice and quiet.

64
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,800
It's written all over your
face that you're happy about it.

65
00:05:00,160 --> 00:05:03,200
I'm just as relieved not
to have to see your face!

66
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:07,260
I'm not getting yelled at every single day either,
so I can finally spend a quiet day.

67
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,860
My luck has finally turned around too!

68
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:18,240
If I can get away from
this troublesome old man,

69
00:05:18,240 --> 00:05:22,160
my management skills should
finally be properly recognized.

70
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:28,740
How sad it is that the Chief
is being demoted and leaving us.

71
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,200
It's a complete abolition and transfer!

72
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,780
Well, that's how it is.

73
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:36,180
Even without me,
I expect you all to cooperate and get along.

74
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:36,580
Yes.

75
00:05:39,980 --> 00:05:41,740
This is the Third Block police box.

76
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:44,420
What a fairly clean police box this is.

77
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,560
But it's difficult here, you know.

78
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:47,580
What do you mean?

79
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,520
I heard it's all young officers,
with no troublemakers like Ryotsu?

80
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,780
The young officers are the problem.

81
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:58,980
The previous team leader wore himself out with stress,
ruined his stomach, and ended up in the hospital.

82
00:06:00,040 --> 00:06:02,060
After all, they're young people these days.

83
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:04,240
They only do what they're told,

84
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,780
and if you scold them, they quit right away.

85
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:09,660
So my true management skills
will be put to the test, I see.

86
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:10,640
Alright!

87
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,740
Gentlemen,

88
00:06:12,740 --> 00:06:16,000
I am Ohara,
the new team leader here as of today.

89
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,300
I look forward to working with you.

90
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:18,460
Otsuka.

91
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:19,440
Sugano.

92
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:20,100
Komagome.

93
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:23,100
Well, you're a bunch of honest young men,
aren't you?

94
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:25,500
There's no need to worry.

95
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:27,088
Yes,

96
00:06:27,138 --> 00:06:31,606
my management policy is to always
make careful situational judgments,

97
00:06:31,656 --> 00:06:33,160
and also be proactive...

98
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,440
Hey, I've got to feed it.

99
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:36,900
It's a Tamagotchi!

100
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,780
and also be bold and decisive...

101
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:41,380
Hello?

102
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,640
Tabata? Now?

103
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,800
Are you all right? It's nothing important.

104
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:48,360
Please go ahead and continue.

105
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:53,360
How embarrassing for a police officer.

106
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,960
You've already beaten it?

107
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:55,420
Seriously?

108
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:56,280
No way, really?

109
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:00,860
It's 11:30, I have to go!

110
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:02,400
Where are you going?

111
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:06,300
There's a super popular spot
that was featured in a magazine.

112
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:10,180
A line forms right away,
so we have to get in line 30 minutes early.

113
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,600
Bonk!

114
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,760
What are you thinking? You're on duty!

115
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,220
Do you have no sense of responsibility?

116
00:07:21,280 --> 00:07:22,860
I quit.

117
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,400
Why should I get yelled at
for something this small,

118
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,760
of all things?

119
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,780
This is ridiculous, right?

120
00:07:28,460 --> 00:07:29,440
You guys

121
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,280
I see, zero management ability

122
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:35,220
That he lacks the ability

123
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,920
and blames it on us.

124
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,640
So that's how it is

125
00:07:40,140 --> 00:07:40,960
N-no way,

126
00:07:41,560 --> 00:07:41,920
that's

127
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:42,940
nonsense.

128
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:50,180
Getting angry at newcomers on their first day would be too petty,
I suppose.

129
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,900
Anyway, let's skip this stiff talk.

130
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,420
How about we go out for drinks tonight?

131
00:07:57,420 --> 00:07:59,280
Don't worry, it's on me.

132
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,400
Tonight?

133
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,060
I've got a show I want to watch.

134
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,080
I've got to clear my game.

135
00:08:05,080 --> 00:08:07,580
Sorry, I'm going to a concert tonight.

136
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:13,220
Besides, when we go drinking,
we'll just go on our own.

137
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:14,460
Please don't go out of your way for us.

138
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:18,180
If you bring the boss-and-subordinate
relationship into our time off, too,

139
00:08:18,180 --> 00:08:19,520
it'll just be a real buzzkill.

140
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:25,360
Does everything have to go at your pace?

141
00:08:26,060 --> 00:08:27,780
When Ryo-chan says he'll treat us,

142
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:30,080
they come running, tails wagging.

143
00:08:35,120 --> 00:08:36,760
What am I thinking?

144
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,920
Now that I've finally
gotten away from the Chief...

145
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,220
We're going to grab a bite too.

146
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:49,120
Chief

147
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:52,080
If it's just the Chief filling in,
then it's lunch break for us.

148
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,900
What? It's already two o'clock, you know.

149
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,340
What's wrong, Ryo-chan?

150
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:56,700
Everything's wrong, that's what.

151
00:08:57,720 --> 00:08:59,880
Every report I handed in has to be redone.

152
00:09:00,580 --> 00:09:01,440
What did you say?

153
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:02,200
What do you mean?

154
00:09:02,520 --> 00:09:04,400
Some didn't have the date filled in,

155
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:06,160
and some didn't have a seal,
so they're all rejected.

156
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:08,840
I got chewed out badly for this, you know.

157
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,260
Isn't this good enough?

158
00:09:10,400 --> 00:09:13,240
But I showed it to Chief Demoshika properly.

159
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:16,040
Damn it, and today's the
release day for the new game!

160
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:16,940
Shit.

161
00:09:18,720 --> 00:09:20,160
Yo, I'm back.

162
00:09:20,580 --> 00:09:21,880
Chief Demoshika.

163
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:25,340
Doesn't this report need the date filled in?

164
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:27,340
Let's see, let's see.

165
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:32,900
Whether this gets filled in or not
doesn't really matter.

166
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,420
Either way is fine, isn't it?

167
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,920
It's fine if you don't,

168
00:09:38,970 --> 00:09:41,880
but it's still better to fill that in,
after all.

169
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:48,080
If I had to say,

170
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:48,620
Damn it!

171
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,833
Because Chief Ohara is so meticulous,

172
00:09:50,883 --> 00:09:53,080
his checks must have been flawless.

173
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,625
Damn it, but,

174
00:09:55,675 --> 00:10:01,180
Chief Ohara would have done it all for me while grumbling,
you know.

175
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,920
Hey, what am I thinking?

176
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:06,525
Ignore those voices and keep moving forward.

177
00:10:06,575 --> 00:10:09,180
The current one is definitely better,
obviously.

178
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:10,990
Yes, eight laps around the park.

179
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:14,310
A blue mini-cycle? It should have
been found at the station, though.

180
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,020
The reports weren't submitted?

181
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:20,660
I handed those to the Chief last week.
Right, Chief?

182
00:10:20,980 --> 00:10:22,842
Yes, I'm holding onto them.

183
00:10:22,892 --> 00:10:25,760
I'll put them away
safely right here for you.

184
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:28,860
Hup! I'll deliver it with all my might!

185
00:10:28,860 --> 00:10:32,560
Ryotsu, you're impatient too.

186
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:39,620
Senpai's working more than ten times harder than usual.
There's no time to slack off at all, is there?

187
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,720
Just turning in paperwork
took up my whole day.

188
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:53,380
I'm back.

189
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,380
Good work, good work.

190
00:10:57,040 --> 00:11:01,940
Another day ended peacefully without any trouble,
didn't it?

191
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,600
You really put me through the wringer.

192
00:11:05,300 --> 00:11:07,660
Fine, I'll let you treat me.

193
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:09,760
What do you say, Chief?

194
00:11:09,760 --> 00:11:11,980
Let's grab a quick drink on the
way home to celebrate the newcomers.

195
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:15,480
To build communication with your subordinates,
nothing beats sake.

196
00:11:15,480 --> 00:11:17,740
There's a great yakitori place.

197
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:19,920
Delicious and cheap.

198
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,200
On you?

199
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,400
No way, I'm not going.

200
00:11:22,820 --> 00:11:24,280
I'm eating at home today.

201
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:25,600
I'm going, then.

202
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:26,240
To Nozaki's.

203
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:35,220
What?

204
00:11:35,220 --> 00:11:35,840
Ryotsu?

205
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,400
Yes.

206
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:38,360
You mean Ryotsu, the Cleanup Queen,

207
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:39,780
you saw him in person, didn't you?

208
00:11:40,120 --> 00:11:41,040
What kind of person is he?

209
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,060
Ryotsu?

210
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:43,560
Well, let's just say...

211
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:45,120
there's no one as outrageous as him.

212
00:11:45,580 --> 00:11:46,920
He's always in sandals,

213
00:11:46,920 --> 00:11:48,680
and he even wears his
uniform on his days off.

214
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:53,380
On the day a game comes out, they drop work
entirely and rush out to buy it first thing.

215
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:55,940
That's cool, isn't it.

216
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,900
Didn't I tell you so?

217
00:11:58,420 --> 00:11:59,860
Cool, you say?

218
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:02,520
Ryo-san is our idol.

219
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,400
Idol.

220
00:12:04,400 --> 00:12:08,600
Being a civil servant yet free from anyone's constraints,
living life on your own terms.

221
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:12,300
It's wonderful, isn't it,
sticking to your own lifestyle like that.

222
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,280
Don't be ridiculous.

223
00:12:14,280 --> 00:12:16,820
That guy just follows
his instincts and desires

224
00:12:16,820 --> 00:12:20,160
without a care for how much
trouble he causes others.

225
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,000
The Chief is way too old-school.

226
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,580
He doesn't understand how we feel at all.

227
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:27,340
That's right.

228
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:31,500
What's wrong with living
your one and only life freely?

229
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,380
Ryotsu-san is our true role model.

230
00:12:34,380 --> 00:12:36,540
A role model? Ryotsu?

231
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:39,180
Apparently he threw the station
chief off the second floor.

232
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:41,220
He's wrecked 53 patrol cars.

233
00:12:41,660 --> 00:12:42,700
Eight at seven o'clock.

234
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:43,280
What happened?

235
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:46,340
I can't understand it at all.

236
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:01,600
Senpai,
you've been looking really pale lately.

237
00:13:02,060 --> 00:13:05,540
Of course I do.
I've already worked over a year's worth.

238
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:07,680
I'm practically the acting chief.

239
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:11,580
You don't even have time to sit in a chair,
let alone slack off.

240
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:15,960
It's a feat that only worked because the
Chief used to manage everything so sharply.

241
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:19,100
With the Chief as he is now,
I'm too uneasy to slack off at all.

242
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:21,540
Stop it.

243
00:13:23,180 --> 00:13:24,480
I'll walk home from here.

244
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,420
I see.

245
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,220
Well then, good night.

246
00:13:41,580 --> 00:13:42,020
Mm.

247
