Chief

263
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:14,420
Why would you,
who never reads books, be here?

264
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:18,840
Chief, you always read nothing but period novels,
and now you're reading business books?

265
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:25,240
Don't tell me you're having trouble with your subordinates,
so you bought that?

266
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:31,440
Hah! No way! They're all good young men.
I have no troubles at all!

267
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:39,840
You're the one who's awkward with the Chief, aren't you?
No way! Work is really easy, and we're totally in sync.

268
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:46,940
I see. Then I've got nothing to worry about,
even as the first official team leader.

269
00:14:46,940 --> 00:14:54,660
That's very welcome! Yes, yes, well then, do your best.
You too, Ryo-chan, I'm counting on you.

270
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,780
Aaaaaah!

271
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:05,760
Mm.

272
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:10,620
Mm.

273
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:20,200
Why are you following me? Chief, don't walk in front of me like that.
I'm going to have a drink at Chidori up ahead.

274
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:21,760
Me too.

275
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,560
Gamoko-san, I won't lose to this guy.

276
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:32,220
Aaaaaah!

277
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:36,200
Woooah!

278
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:37,360
Aaaaaah!

279
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:39,140
Eeeeeeh!

280
00:15:39,140 --> 00:15:39,720
Eeeeeeh

281
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:42,840
Eeeeeeh

282
00:15:47,520 --> 00:15:49,080
Aaaaaah

283
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,860
Welcome! Is it two of you?

284
00:15:51,860 --> 00:15:52,780
Just one.

285
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:55,180
I'm terribly sorry, but

286
00:15:55,860 --> 00:15:57,880
this is the only seat we have open.

287
00:15:58,680 --> 00:15:59,680
Your companions' names?

288
00:15:59,680 --> 00:16:00,280
Beer.

289
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:00,900
Coming right up!

290
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,940
Here you go, pal!

291
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:15,820
Ever since I became Chief, my stomach's
been doing better, so the sake tastes great.

292
00:16:17,260 --> 00:16:21,040
With no idiot subordinates around,
every day is so fulfilling.

293
00:16:21,400 --> 00:16:22,780
What would you like for snacks?

294
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:26,700
Let's get two each of liver,
shiro, and tsukune.

295
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,180
Ugh, you're so stingy.

296
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:34,420
I'll have liver, shiro, tsukune, cartilage,
small intestine, tongue, heart, head, and tsunagi too.

297
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:40,780
Add one serving of yosenabe
to the sashimi platter.

298
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:45,300
Eeeeeh, for us, a large sashimi
plate and two servings of yosenabe.

299
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,360
and kimchi rabe.

300
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:49,620
Fugu chiri, yudofu,
Ishikari nabe, and cold tofu.

301
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:52,920
Aji no tataki, curry karaage,
grilled whole squid, and nikujaga.

302
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:56,360
Pickles, shirasu oroshi,
and sake-steamed clams.

303
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:59,160
Agedashi tofu, edamame,
tatami iwashi, and shiokara.

304
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:03,440
Pig's trotters, tako butsu,
good beer, and a big tokkuri of sake.

305
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,680
So, sake, please.

306
00:17:15,020 --> 00:17:16,260
My head hurts.

307
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,380
I did something stupid yesterday.

308
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:22,760
But I just can't remember
anything after the Chidori part.

309
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:25,480
So, in the rare-goods joke series,
you see...

310
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:28,920
This "soul" part is different, you know.

311
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,080
That's true.

312
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:32,560
What on earth are you thinking?

313
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:36,280
Emergency call, emergency call.

314
00:17:36,640 --> 00:17:39,060
Armed robbery at the
Hotsudo Bank in 2-chome.

315
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:42,220
The suspects are fleeing on a
motorcycle toward Kameari 3-chome.

316
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:43,120
Repeat.

317
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:45,360
Otsuka-kun, Sugaki-kun, Komagome-kun.

318
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,360
Just as you heard.

319
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:47,800
Let's catch them in the patrol car.

320
00:17:48,840 --> 00:17:50,540
But our shift is almost over.

321
00:17:50,540 --> 00:17:52,680
I have a date planned.

322
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,080
Stop your whining.

323
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:54,960
Follow me.

324
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:04,740
Aaaaaah!

325
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:08,980
Eeeeeeh!

326
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:12,600
Damn it!

327
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,120
k

328
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,980
Move aside, please, excuse me!

329
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,460
What a streaker!

330
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:34,500
Ryo-san suddenly darted out!

331
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:36,240
You should be more careful too, you know!

332
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,280
What are you doing in a place like this?

333
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:41,100
I'm the real Ryo-san!

334
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,020
Super lucky!

335
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:43,220
What's with you guys?

336
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:45,920
Ryo-san is our ideal, you know.

337
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,900
I'm your ideal?

338
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:50,700
Your subordinates seem to have a better eye for people,
don't they?

339
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,560
We don't have time for this!

340
00:18:55,560 --> 00:18:57,600
Let's go! Don't dawdle, Ryotsu!

341
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,640
I'm not your subordinate.

342
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:01,180
Don't give me orders.

343
00:19:03,300 --> 00:19:03,940
Come.

344
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:05,540
Fine, fine, I get it.

345
00:19:05,540 --> 00:19:06,840
Just tell us, then.

346
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,160
That Ryotsu-san...

347
00:19:08,680 --> 00:19:11,060
is totally submissive to Chief Ohara.

348
00:19:11,060 --> 00:19:12,000
Could it be that

349
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,420
Chief Ohara is an amazing person?

350
00:19:15,260 --> 00:19:15,660
This is

351
00:19:17,240 --> 00:19:19,000
definitely the suspects' motorcycle.

352
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:23,340
Judging by the direction of this bike,
the suspects went this way.

353
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:25,180
Considering the skid marks, too,

354
00:19:29,240 --> 00:19:30,100
This way!

355
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:33,240
Don't copy me!

356
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:35,040
You're the one copying me!

357
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:37,860
Chief, it's cramped in here, so move aside!

358
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,320
You're the one who should step back!

359
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,700
Help!

360
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:43,860
What?

361
00:19:44,420 --> 00:19:45,400
Somebody help!

362
00:19:47,440 --> 00:19:49,300
Help! Somebody, help!

363
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:51,800
Let that person go!

364
00:19:52,080 --> 00:19:53,180
Get a car ready!

365
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:55,680
Who knows what a samurai might do?

366
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:57,740
Let's call for backup right away.

367
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:58,740
What did you say?

368
00:19:59,340 --> 00:20:02,180
Wait! We mustn't provoke the suspect.

369
00:20:02,820 --> 00:20:04,660
But it's just us, though.

370
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:07,000
The hostage's safety comes first.

371
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:11,100
Still, what should we do?

372
00:20:11,940 --> 00:20:13,240
Where's Ryo-san?

373
00:20:14,860 --> 00:20:16,760
At a time like this, where did that guy go?

374
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:19,080
Over there.

375
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,920
What are you dawdling for, you bastard?

376
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:28,780
He's going to pounce on us from above.

377
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:30,260
Quiet.

378
00:20:42,340 --> 00:20:43,020
No good.

379
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:43,880
Hey!

380
00:20:45,320 --> 00:20:46,220
Don't come any closer!

381
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:48,780
Don't worry, we won't do anything.

382
00:20:48,780 --> 00:20:50,020
Help me!

383
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,100
See? We're unarmed.

384
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:54,740
Let's hear what you have to say.

385
00:20:54,740 --> 00:20:57,740
Liar, you're hiding something under your clothes,
aren't you?

386
00:21:10,800 --> 00:21:23,280
No good.

387
00:21:23,770 --> 00:21:25,040
Look!

388
00:21:28,600 --> 00:21:31,460
How's this? I'm not hiding anything.

389
00:21:31,460 --> 00:21:33,280
I didn't expect him to go that far.

390
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:36,640
He still has punch left.

391
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:38,620
What's wrong?

392
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:42,940
I bet you're hiding your
brains in your underwear.

393
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:43,820
Damn it.

394
00:21:45,180 --> 00:21:47,000
Okay, calm down.

395
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:47,740
Shut up.

396
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,800
Now! Let's go!

397
00:22:00,220 --> 00:22:01,380
Don't let go, Ryotsu!

398
00:22:01,380 --> 00:22:03,580
Hurry!

399
00:22:05,380 --> 00:22:06,180
Hold on!

400
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:32,680
!

401
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:40,500
Please stop with the reckless stunts, Chief!

402
00:22:40,500 --> 00:22:44,660
Your sturdy body is the
only useful thing about you.

403
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:49,740
I haven't moved around like that in ages,
so I'm really exhausted.

404
00:22:49,740 --> 00:22:51,620
You're getting on in years too, Chief.

405
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:55,660
What are you talking about? As long
as troublemakers like you are around,

406
00:22:55,660 --> 00:22:56,940
I can't let myself slow down.

407
00:22:56,940 --> 00:22:58,980
Chief, we're deeply moved!

408
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:01,280
You're amazing, Chief.

409
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:03,840
From now on, we'll follow you, Chief.

410
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,260
Just tell us whatever you need.

411
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:06,040
Yes, sir!

412
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:07,560
I see.

413
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,000
But, all of you,

414
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,220
what matters most is teamwork.

415
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:13,540
You must know each other's strengths

416
00:23:13,540 --> 00:23:16,280
and never forget to make up
for each other's weaknesses.

417
00:23:16,280 --> 00:23:16,840
Yes.

418
00:23:17,280 --> 00:23:18,800
That was a terrible ordeal.

419
00:23:19,180 --> 00:23:22,340
Don't you dare come back to the
Kōen-mae police box ever again!

420
00:23:24,360 --> 00:23:26,500
Bakabōn!

421
00:23:27,540 --> 00:23:29,000
What is this report?

422
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,080
What were you all doing while I was away?

423
00:23:31,080 --> 00:23:34,360
No, that part is up to you,
whether the Chief writes it or not...

424
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:39,160
How many years have you been a cop, anyway?

425
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:40,860
Right back to this

426
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:42,620
But we need this voice, don't we.

427
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:46,380
Yeah, it just doesn't feel like the Kameari Park police box,
does it?

428
00:23:46,380 --> 00:23:48,480
Do you think it's fine to be
half-assed about everything?

429
00:23:48,480 --> 00:23:49,860
I'm not being half-assed.

430
00:23:49,860 --> 00:23:52,040
It's because you're too stubborn, Chief!

431
00:23:52,040 --> 00:23:53,600
Stubbornness is in my nature.

432
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:55,740
Rewrite the report properly.

433
00:23:55,740 --> 00:23:57,340
Don't shout in my ear.

434
00:23:57,340 --> 00:23:58,580
I can hear you just fine.

435
00:23:58,580 --> 00:24:00,100
No matter how many times I say it,
you still don't get it.

436
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,580
Honda, quit moping around forever!

437
00:24:06,900 --> 00:24:08,740
Getting dumped happens all the time,
doesn't it?

438
00:24:08,740 --> 00:24:12,540
The more heartbreaks a man has,
the kinder he becomes, you know.

439
00:24:12,540 --> 00:24:13,560
That's what I was trying to say.

440
00:24:13,960 --> 00:24:15,200
Great, now he's even more depressed.

441
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,840
Hey, pull yourself together, Honda!

442
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:17,500
Hey.

443
00:24:18,080 --> 00:24:21,080
Next time:
"Run, Heartbroken Rider." See you then!

444
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:37,160
People gossip that I'm a woman who can't fall in love,
but

445
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:42,900
I have so many things I want to do.

446
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:52,020
I want to ride a motorbike
across the vast desert.

447
00:24:52,020 --> 00:24:58,960
I want to be freer than a bird.

448
00:25:00,200 --> 00:25:07,120
A lady's dreams change
as fast as a kaleidoscope.

449
00:25:09,100 --> 00:25:15,240
My heart says, "Sorry, wait for me."

450
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:22,220
The panoramic future
will soon be dazzling too.

451
00:25:23,460 --> 00:25:30,100
You understand, right? Sorry, wait for me.

